# Burner small: a flat electric burner on the glass hob, 8.4 m across and 0.16 m thick (60 times life size: a 2.7 mm coil; 28 says 0.02 m, which does not mesh at 256 cells
# without 50k triangles), origin at its middle, resting on y = 0. Cold it is dark cast steel (kitchen_burner): concentric coils round a plate, the glass showing between them.
# The heat (0 cold to 1 hot) is not part of the model: 28.10 writes it per vertex to the vertices of the kitchen_burner material for the ember glow (the materials have no
# emission yet, 30.1). No collider; the burner is a navmesh area, a scout walks over the coil.
format 1
collider none

# Detail 0.3, not 0.15: at 0.15 the default 128 cells gave cells of 0.2-0.25 m, thicker than the 0.16 m burner, so no sample was inside it
Detail detail=0.3
    Material material=kitchen_burner
        Translate translation=(0, 0.08, 0)
            Union
                Subtraction
                    CappedCylinder radius=4.2 height=0.08
                    CappedCylinder radius=3.7 height=0.2
                Subtraction
                    CappedCylinder radius=3.3 height=0.08
                    CappedCylinder radius=2.9 height=0.2
                Subtraction
                    CappedCylinder radius=2.5 height=0.08
                    CappedCylinder radius=2.1 height=0.2
                Subtraction
                    CappedCylinder radius=1.7 height=0.08
                    CappedCylinder radius=1.3 height=0.2
                CappedCylinder radius=0.8 height=0.08
